title: Fix ternary mixed-fallible-arm phi ICE + struct-return bugs
status: complete
atomic: true
priority: high
blocked_by: []
created_at: '2026-06-15T12:26:54'
updated_at: '2026-06-15T13:13:02'
result: 'Fixed all 3 codegen/typer bugs. (1) Ternary mixed-fallible-arm phi ICE: added
  reconcile_ternary_arms in src/typer/expr/quaternary.rs, called from expr/mod.rs
  ternary lowering — propagates the fallible arm to its ok-inner type when arms''
  fallible-ness differs inside a fallible fn. (2)+(3) Shared root cause: parser turns
  single-uppercase-letter type names into Type::Param, so a struct named P made `*mk
  returns P` look generic (monomorphized to mk__G_i64, ret type collapsed to i64 ->
  zeroed struct return + non-exhaustive-match-on-I64). Fixed by pre-scanning declared
  type/enum/err/actor/store names into Typer.declared_type_names and making effective_type_params/is_generic_fn/normalize_generic_fn
  instance methods that filter declared names. +3 conformance tests in tests/error_effects.rs
  (ternary_mixed_fallible_arm_reconciles, plain_struct_return_payload_intact, match_on_fallible_struct_return).
  Zero warnings; full suite green except 3 pre-existing unrelated @column failures.'
description: 'Three related codegen/typer bugs found making log_ingest.jn idiomatic
  (v108). (1) ICE mir_codegen/mod.rs:633 phi mismatch when a ternary `cond ? <plain
  i64> ! <fallible call>` mixes an i64 arm with a Result<i64,E> arm — typer must unify
  both arms to the fn''s fallible result (auto-wrap-ok the plain arm, propagate the
  fallible arm) before the phi. (2) non-fallible bare struct return `*mk returns P\n
  P(1,2)` returns zeroed fields (sret bug). (3) `match` on a fallible struct return
  reports ''non-exhaustive match on I64''. See memory bug_ternary_mixed_fallible_arm_phi_ice
  and bug_bare_struct_return_zeroed. DoD: minimal repros compile+run correctly, conformance
  tests added to tests/error_effects.rs, zero warnings, full suite green.'
